1
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:16,349
‎OCTOBER 15, 1890

2
00:00:17,684 --> 00:00:20,311
<i>‎The competitors
‎are now entering the Rocky Mountains</i>

3
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:24,065
<i>‎as they make their way to Cañon City!</i>

4
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:28,319
<i>‎The greatest obstacle in the third stage</i>

5
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:31,781
<i>‎is the majestic Rocky Mountains!</i>

6
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:36,202
‎How they cross them could be the key!

7
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,292
‎This is bad. Really bad!

8
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:47,005
‎I'll definitely finish first
‎in the third stage,

9
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:49,507
‎but that'll only bring me to 136 points.

10
00:00:49,591 --> 00:00:52,802
‎That bastard Dio already has 150 points.

11
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:55,472
‎I still won't take the overall lead.

12
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>‎Worse yet...</i>

13
00:00:58,224 --> 00:00:59,809
<i>‎Johnny!</i>

14
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:02,562
<i>‎If he finishes first,
‎he'll have 180 points</i>

15
00:01:02,645 --> 00:01:04,773
<i>‎and take the lead outright!</i>

16
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:07,984
<i>‎He promised he'd finish behind me!</i>

17
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:10,570
<i>‎What a backstabbing liar!</i>

18
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,697
<i>‎I'll make him pay!</i>

19
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:16,618
‎Besides, Dio and Sand Man
‎are already ahead.

20
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:20,955
‎There's no way they'll end this stage
‎with zero points.

21
00:01:21,915 --> 00:01:24,417
‎Sure would be nice if they did...

22
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:26,127
‎Gyro, look!

23
00:01:26,211 --> 00:01:27,212
‎Huh?

24
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:30,256
‎Dio's down over there.

25
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:35,178
‎Something doesn't look right.

26
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,639
‎Let me see.

27
00:01:42,018 --> 00:01:44,813
‎Looks like he was thrown from his horse.

28
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:47,607
‎He's bleeding from his face.

29
00:01:47,690 --> 00:01:51,069
<i>‎Yes! Maybe this is my lucky day...</i>

30
00:01:51,152 --> 00:01:53,780
‎Dio was thrown from his horse?

31
00:01:53,863 --> 00:01:55,865
‎Hard to believe.

32
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:57,909
‎He's curled up.

33
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:02,872
‎Looks like he'll be delayed for a while.

34
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:05,250
‎He may even have to drop out.

35
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:06,793
‎Let's keep moving, Gyro.

36
00:02:06,876 --> 00:02:10,004
‎Oh? Coming from you, Johnny?

37
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:13,675
‎I'm no stranger
‎to enjoying someone else's bad luck,

38
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:16,970
‎but he could have
‎life-threatening injuries.

39
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:18,888
‎Let's check on him.

40
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:22,308
‎You shouldn't go near Diego Brando, Gyro.

41
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:27,188
‎You're pretty petty, aren't you?

42
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:29,149
‎He can't be trusted.

43
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:34,195
‎He's a brilliant jockey
‎in Britain's prestigious racing circuit.

44
00:02:34,279 --> 00:02:38,533
‎But he'll stop at nothing
‎for money and victory.

45
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,119
‎Shady rumors follow him.

46
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,955
<i>‎For example, when he was 20,</i>

47
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:49,544
<i>‎he married an 83-year-old woman
‎for her fortune.</i>

48
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:57,218
<i>‎She died six months later.</i>

49
00:02:57,969 --> 00:03:00,179
<i>‎Some even say Dio killed her.</i>

50
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:05,310
‎So you're saying...

51
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:09,147
‎This could all be an act to fool us.

52
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:13,109
‎He's the kind of man who could
‎even be involved with terrorists.

53
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:21,576
‎Maybe if he were losing to someone
‎who knew all that.

54
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:24,704
‎But he's in first place.
‎Why would he do that?

55
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:26,581
‎I'll go take a look.

56
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,182
‎Hey, Dio. You okay?

57
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:46,476
‎Need a rescue team? Say the word.

58
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:47,852
‎I'll call one for you.

59
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,536
<i>‎What's with his fingers?</i>

60
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:10,208
<i>‎Scabs? Did he touch something?</i>

61
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:13,628
‎Mind your own business.

62
00:04:13,711 --> 00:04:16,256
‎Quit wasting time and go.

63
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:20,260
‎It'll be this Dio
‎who passes you in the end.

64
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,472
‎Looks like you're fine.

65
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:25,974
‎Good to hear!

66
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:33,439
‎Let's go, Johnny.

67
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:36,150
‎Right.

68
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,811
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

69
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:31,432
{\an8}‎3RD STAGE -DAY 5- THE ROCKY MOUNTAINS
‎ABOUT 240 MILES FROM MONUMENT VALLEY

70
00:06:31,974 --> 00:06:33,601
{\an8}‎FRIGHTENING MONSTERS, PART 1

71
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:36,979
{\an8}‎Gyro! We'll cross the Rocky Mountains
‎in two days!

72
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,441
‎There!
‎That mountain's right on the course!

73
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:43,986
‎About nine miles away.
‎Shall we make it there today?

74
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,154
‎Not today!

75
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:48,574
‎It'll be dark soon. The horses need rest.

76
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,661
<i>‎No doubt about it.</i>

77
00:06:51,744 --> 00:06:54,205
<i>‎The next piece is on that mountain.</i>

78
00:06:55,206 --> 00:06:57,083
<i>‎I'll know once I get there!</i>

79
00:06:57,166 --> 00:06:58,209
‎Hey, Johnny.

80
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,628
‎My horse is scared.

81
00:07:06,092 --> 00:07:07,510
‎Johnny, look!

82
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:08,970
‎It's Dio!

83
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:15,810
‎You're looking a lot stronger than before.

84
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:17,145
‎Stay sharp, Johnny!

85
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:20,398
‎Don't let him pass us!

86
00:07:20,982 --> 00:07:23,484
‎Easy, you two. You've got it all wrong.

87
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:26,237
‎We're done for today. It'll be dark soon.

88
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,990
‎There's a small village up ahead.

89
00:07:29,073 --> 00:07:30,700
‎We can spend the night there.

90
00:07:30,783 --> 00:07:35,413
‎We'd better not camp out.
‎There are wild animals around here.

91
00:07:36,664 --> 00:07:40,418
‎The other evening,
‎I was surrounded by wild animals,

92
00:07:40,501 --> 00:07:43,421
‎by several cougars and rattlesnakes.

93
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:48,676
‎They blocked the trail
‎and I couldn't get past.

94
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,888
‎I tried to go around them,

95
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:55,892
‎but one of them
‎actually stepped aside for me.

96
00:07:55,975 --> 00:07:59,061
‎How polite of it. An animal, no less.

97
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:02,356
‎Which animal do you think let me through?

98
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:05,276
‎The cougars? Or the rattlesnakes?

99
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:07,737
‎The answer is...

100
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:09,572
‎The rattlesnakes!

101
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:11,866
‎Did you get it?

102
00:08:11,949 --> 00:08:14,410
‎It wasn't that rattled after all!

103
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,328
‎Huh?

104
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:18,623
‎Come on, it's a quiz.

105
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:20,124
‎Just a little quiz.

106
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:23,794
‎Then the cougars
‎could eat me on the trail!

107
00:08:23,878 --> 00:08:25,379
‎"Horse d'oeuvre!"

108
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:29,258
‎Then all the cougars go, "Horse d'oeuvre!"

109
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:32,887
‎I feel fantastic!

110
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:36,766
‎I've never felt better! I love it!

111
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:39,310
‎Maybe that fall did it.

112
00:08:39,393 --> 00:08:42,939
‎I feel light as a feather!
‎Too bad the sun's going down!

113
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:46,234
‎Diego Brando! Stay away from us!

114
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:47,610
‎We're not going with you!

115
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:50,446
‎Johnny Joestar...

116
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:54,992
‎You rode brilliantly
‎in both the first and second stages.

117
00:08:55,076 --> 00:08:58,871
‎I heard you were injured,
‎but you've made an incredible comeback!

118
00:09:09,173 --> 00:09:10,508
‎Ha!

119
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:14,011
‎If you're such great riders,
‎can you do this?

120
00:09:19,225 --> 00:09:22,228
‎Hey, Johnny. What's gotten into him?

121
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:26,732
‎Are all brilliant jockeys this crazy?

122
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,651
‎Beats me!

123
00:09:28,734 --> 00:09:30,152
‎Something's not right.

124
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,822
‎Are we really staying with him tonight?

125
00:09:32,905 --> 00:09:34,740
‎Even if I don't want to...

126
00:09:35,533 --> 00:09:38,703
‎He's got a point.
‎There are wolves around here too.

127
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,496
‎We need to stay in the village.

128
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,082
‎Exactly! It's safer.

129
00:09:43,165 --> 00:09:45,126
‎The wolves hunt in packs!

130
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,837
‎He can hear us.

131
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,677
‎Welcome!

132
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,765
‎-Welcome!
‎-We've been expecting you!

133
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:02,810
‎They sure know a lot about the race,

134
00:10:02,893 --> 00:10:05,771
‎even way out here.

135
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:09,191
‎Where's Dio? He's gone!

136
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,484
‎Who knows?

137
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:13,738
‎Maybe he's off greeting the villagers.

138
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,324
‎I'm serious.

139
00:10:16,407 --> 00:10:19,201
‎I'm not sleeping anywhere near him.

140
00:10:19,285 --> 00:10:23,247
‎He's the most despicable jockey alive.

141
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:26,292
‎He'd poison a horse's feed
‎or sabotage someone's tack

142
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:28,377
‎without a second thought.

143
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:30,338
‎I know.

144
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:34,550
‎We'll guard the horses and food,
‎just like when we camp out.

145
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:37,011
‎There's a fireplace.

146
00:10:37,094 --> 00:10:39,930
‎Let's make supper.
‎I'll gather some firewood.

147
00:11:05,915 --> 00:11:07,208
<i>‎Dio...</i>

148
00:11:29,522 --> 00:11:31,732
‎That's coffee.

149
00:11:33,025 --> 00:11:35,111
‎I can smell it.

150
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,779
‎Smells wonderful.

151
00:11:37,446 --> 00:11:39,990
‎What are you doing over there, Dio?

152
00:11:40,074 --> 00:11:42,952
‎-Nothing.
‎-"Nothing"?

153
00:11:44,036 --> 00:11:46,497
‎Hey! Don't come in!

154
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:51,585
‎Oh. Is this because I was eating rocks?

155
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:57,216
‎Didn't you know?
‎They're for digestion, Mr. Joestar.

156
00:11:57,299 --> 00:11:59,885
‎They grind up food in your stomach.

157
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:01,720
‎They're called gastroliths.

158
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:04,723
‎Most meat-eaters do it.

159
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:09,019
‎Healthy habit.
‎I took a cue from birds and crocodiles.

160
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:11,981
‎You're making coffee, aren't you?

161
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:15,067
‎It doesn't smell like Blue Mountain,

162
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,194
‎but it smells great.

163
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,738
‎Mind if I have a cup?

164
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,991
‎How are you after that fall?

165
00:12:22,074 --> 00:12:24,160
‎You looked badly hurt.

166
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:26,662
‎I feel great.

167
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:28,205
‎I'm perfectly fine.

168
00:12:28,289 --> 00:12:30,082
‎Why do you keep the gloves on?

169
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:33,085
‎It's October in the Rockies.
‎Nights get cold.

170
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,129
‎I take them off to wash my hands.

171
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:37,840
‎Now, how about that coffee? Come on.

172
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:41,927
‎I don't want to travel with you.
‎Just so we're clear.

173
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:46,807
‎It's right in front of you.
‎Drink it, then find another empty house.

174
00:12:54,231 --> 00:12:56,901
‎Uh... can I ask you something?

175
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:59,528
‎Which one should I drink?

176
00:13:00,112 --> 00:13:02,823
‎What do you mean? There's only one cup.

177
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:06,410
‎Dio... don't tell me you can't see it.

178
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:07,745
‎The rest is canned food.

179
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,872
‎Can't see?

180
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:12,291
‎Don't insult me!

181
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:15,419
‎I can see just fine.

182
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:17,838
‎My eyes and body are in perfect shape.

183
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:20,257
‎I see even better at night.

184
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,510
‎So... which one is it?

185
00:13:23,802 --> 00:13:25,179
‎Which one?

186
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:30,226
‎Hey! I told you, there's only one cup!

187
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:35,940
‎Weird guy.

188
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:45,324
‎What's that? Teeth?

189
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:48,035
<i>‎What the hell is he?</i>

190
00:13:48,118 --> 00:13:50,037
<i>‎What's under that bandage?</i>

191
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,581
<i>‎It's a mouth!</i>

192
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,250
<i>‎It reaches his ears!</i>

193
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:56,502
<i>‎That mouth... it's just like...</i>

194
00:13:56,585 --> 00:13:58,420
‎What are you doing, Johnny?

195
00:13:59,338 --> 00:14:01,924
‎There sure are a lot of flies.

196
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,717
‎They're coming through the window.

197
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,136
‎Close it.

198
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:18,065
‎Johnny! Shut the window now!

199
00:14:18,148 --> 00:14:21,026
‎Forget the flies! Didn't you notice?

200
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,237
‎Something's nearby!

201
00:14:24,446 --> 00:14:25,865
‎A dead bear!

202
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:27,491
‎Something's been eating it!

203
00:14:27,575 --> 00:14:30,077
‎No human did this!

204
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,209
‎Dio!

205
00:14:44,049 --> 00:14:46,051
‎What the hell is he?

206
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:49,096
‎He transformed!

207
00:14:49,179 --> 00:14:52,099
‎Dio... He's a Stand user!

208
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:59,440
‎Gyro!

209
00:15:06,864 --> 00:15:08,198
<i>‎Tusk!</i>

210
00:15:10,367 --> 00:15:11,368
<i>‎He dodged it?</i>

211
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:21,587
‎Dio's an enemy!
‎He really is with the terrorists!

212
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:34,975
‎Well, well... What incredible eyesight.

213
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:38,270
‎From this close...

214
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:40,981
‎and you made it look easy.

215
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,745
‎Gyro! Above you!

216
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,460
‎Is your goal

217
00:16:01,543 --> 00:16:03,837
‎to find the next corpse?

218
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:07,091
‎Or are you here to kill us and take ours?

219
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:09,551
‎You're too quick to react.

220
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:12,805
‎But if something moves slowly...

221
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:15,766
‎you won't think you need to dodge.

222
00:16:27,569 --> 00:16:30,614
‎I put my Steel Ball in that can.

223
00:16:30,698 --> 00:16:33,951
‎How I got it through the metal...
‎that's a secret.

224
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:39,999
‎Gyro!

225
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:44,962
‎Doesn't look like it did much.

226
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,672
‎Let's get out of here, Johnny!

227
00:16:47,756 --> 00:16:50,426
‎Get outside, now!

228
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,891
‎What is he?

229
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,601
‎A Stand ability like this!

230
00:16:59,685 --> 00:17:01,729
‎What kind of ability is that?

231
00:17:01,812 --> 00:17:03,814
‎It's a dinosaur, Johnny!

232
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:07,901
‎Looks like Dio's gained the powers
‎of a dinosaur.

233
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:10,696
‎Dinosaur? What's a dinosaur?

234
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:11,905
‎You don't know?

235
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:15,993
‎They're enormous creatures!
‎Bigger than African elephants!

236
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:20,706
‎A scientist named Owen
‎coined the word "dinosaur."

237
00:17:21,665 --> 00:17:23,333
‎This one's smaller, though.

238
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,002
‎Forget that!

239
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:29,089
‎Anyway, they lived on Earth
‎long before humans!

240
00:17:29,173 --> 00:17:32,718
‎Why does Dio have the powers
‎of an ancient creature?

241
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:35,220
‎Maybe it's connected to fossils.

242
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:39,141
‎Ever since they were discovered
‎in Colorado's cliffs,

243
00:17:39,224 --> 00:17:41,602
‎fossils have turned up
‎all over the Rockies!

244
00:18:09,004 --> 00:18:11,715
‎Damn it! The door won't hold!

245
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:13,383
‎We're going down the cliff!

246
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:15,010
‎No! I'm not going!

247
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:19,056
‎If Dio's after the corpse,
‎I have to take him down!

248
00:18:19,681 --> 00:18:21,475
‎Instead... don't move an inch!

249
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:24,269
‎Dio can't see you if you stay still!

250
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,354
‎What?

251
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:35,239
‎Don't move at all, Gyro.

252
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:39,701
‎For some reason,
‎Dio only sees things that move.

253
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:41,870
‎Maybe that's how dinosaurs are.

254
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:55,217
‎Don't move! Don't even blink.

255
00:18:56,009 --> 00:18:58,762
‎I'm convinced. It happened before.

256
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,682
‎He couldn't see the coffee.

257
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:07,396
‎Great!

258
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,940
‎He thinks we went down the cliff.

259
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:21,535
‎Hey, did he spot us?

260
00:19:21,618 --> 00:19:22,786
‎He's coming back!

261
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:31,503
‎Easy, Gyro.

262
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,213
‎He doesn't know.

263
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:35,966
‎He's just sniffing the bear.

264
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:51,315
‎Did it work?

265
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:54,067
‎Where'd he go? Did he leave?

266
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:57,696
‎Do you think he lost us?

267
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:07,372
<i>‎That's it! He knows!</i>

268
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:11,585
<i>‎Dio already saw what the Steel Ball can do
‎in the first stage!</i>

269
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:14,254
‎Gyro, this is bad!

270
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:19,301
‎He knows your spinning Steel Ball
‎always comes back to you!

271
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:21,261
‎He knows where it'll end up!

272
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:24,765
‎He'll follow the Steel Ball!

273
00:20:30,854 --> 00:20:33,148
‎No!

274
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:46,245
‎Calm down, Johnny.

275
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:51,124
‎The Steel Ball came back
‎and flattened my legs with its spin.

276
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:57,547
‎Looks like Dio thinks
‎we went behind the wall.

277
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:03,553
‎Yes! He went down the cliff!

278
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:08,934
‎Johnny, about those letters
‎on your left arm...

279
00:21:09,017 --> 00:21:10,727
‎I just realized something.

280
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:14,106
‎About the way they're arranged.

281
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:27,786
‎Gyro!

282
00:21:27,869 --> 00:21:30,038
‎Something's wrong.

283
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:37,170
‎Do you hear something below us?

284
00:21:37,796 --> 00:21:40,632
‎Yeah. What's making that noise?

285
00:21:43,593 --> 00:21:45,262
‎What? What's this?

286
00:21:50,851 --> 00:21:52,227
‎What?

287
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:56,273
‎It's transformed too!
‎And it's still alive!

288
00:21:56,356 --> 00:21:59,568
‎Just what is Dio's ability?

289
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:35,914
{\an8}‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke

